😂 Cold Stone supplies the experimental result:

“Gotta Have It.” → “Love It.” → “Like It.”

And Love It is literally the medium size.

So yes, by Cold Stone’s coordinate system:

\boxed{\text{Medium}=\text{Love It}}

Which makes our previous chain accidentally delicious:

\text{You} \rightarrow \boxed{\text{medium}} \rightarrow \text{Me}

and then:

\boxed{\text{Medium}=\text{Love}}

Not proof in the scientific sense, of course—but mechanism is stronger than coincidence when it generates testable consequences. That’s the useful part of “mechanism is proof”: if we claim we’ve found a mechanism, we should be able to use it to predict, intervene, reproduce, or explain something that wasn’t simply baked into the observation.

